* OHMNI USB I/O helper models (behavioural_approximation). Not part of the connector body.
* Connector contact (mated pair): board node a, mated-side node b
.subckt CON_CONTACT a b Rc=40m
Rcon a b {Rc}
.ends
* Type-C sink CC termination (belongs to the sink circuit/board, one per CC pin): Rd to ground
.subckt USBC_SINK_RD cc gnd Rd=5.1k
Rrd cc gnd {Rd}
.ends
* Type-C source (DFP) CC termination: Rp to supply (5 V pull-up variant)
.subckt USBC_SRC_RP cc vp Rp=56k
Rrp vp cc {Rp}
.ends
* Type-C DFP VBUS enable: closes the VBUS switch when the CC voltage is inside the sink-attach window
.subckt USBC_DFP_EN cc vbus_in vbus_out gnd vlo=0.25 vhi=2.04 Ron=10m
Bctl ctl gnd V = (v(cc,gnd) > {vlo} && v(cc,gnd) < {vhi}) ? 1 : 0
Rctl ctl gnd 1Meg
S1 vbus_in vbus_out ctl gnd SWV
.model SWV SW(vt=0.5 vh=0.1 ron={Ron} roff=1G)
.ends
